    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "> There is no performance problem involve here\n\n100% agree\n\n> and it makes the code easier to grasp (no if)\n\nThis is true only if you know what is lodash.identity. The first time I encountered this kind of code I wondered \"What is identity doing?\". Then I had to go to the lodash documentation and find identity documentation only to understand that it was doing nothing at all (a noop with a return).\n\nI rarely use noop() and identity(), only in cases for example an API forces me to pass a parameter while I do not have the usage of it (eg a library force passing a listener that I will not use).\n\nHere we do control the code and still, we are executing a function while we know there's nothing to do at all. So yes it seems to make the implementation code smarter but in the end it's a bit lying, a simple if would make the code exhaustive without having to use and understand lodash.identity.\n\nThis is really a detail and not linked to the awesomeness of the feature in the PR but I wanted to explain the reasoning here.\n\nThis do not restrict us to just merge this and move on.\n",
    "commit_id": "0df05a8cf88f0e96a4a70a0f96138d5536ff3dc4",
    "created_at": "2015-09-23T07:23:19Z",
